<h1>Viewing User Profiles</h1>

<p>The user profile page displays comprehensive information about a StarExec user account, including personal details, community memberships, resource quotas, and owned solvers, benchmarks, and jobs.</p>

<h2>Profile Information</h2>

<p>At the top of the user profile, you can see:</p>

<ul>
	<li><strong>Profile Picture:</strong> The user's avatar image</li>
	<li><strong>Email Address:</strong> Contact information for the user</li>
	<li><strong>Institution:</strong> The user's affiliated organization</li>
	<li><strong>Member Since:</strong> The date the account was created</li>
	<li><strong>Member Type:</strong> The user's role (regular user, developer, or administrator)</li>
	<li><strong>Websites:</strong> Any websites associated with the user's profile</li>
</ul>

<h2>Communities</h2>

<p>This section displays all communities that the user is a member of. Communities provide collaborative spaces for sharing and managing solvers and benchmarks.</p>

<h2>User Quotas</h2>

<p>If you are viewing your own profile or have administrative privileges, you can see resource quota information:</p>

<ul>
	<li><strong>Disk Quota:</strong> The maximum disk space the user can use</li>
	<li><strong>Current Disk Usage:</strong> The amount of disk space currently being used</li>
	<li><strong>Job Pair Quota:</strong> The maximum number of job pairs the user can own</li>
	<li><strong>Job Pairs Owned:</strong> The current number of job pairs owned by the user</li>
</ul>

<h2>Solvers, Benchmarks, and Jobs</h2>

<p>The profile displays tables of the user's resources:</p>

<ul>
	<li><strong>Solvers:</strong> Solver programs uploaded or owned by the user</li>
	<li><strong>Benchmarks:</strong> Test problems uploaded or owned by the user</li>
	<li><strong>Uploads:</strong> Batch uploads of benchmarks with their completion status</li>
	<li><strong>Jobs:</strong> Computational jobs created by the user, showing their status and statistics</li>
</ul>

<h2>User Actions</h2>

<p>If you are viewing your own profile, you can perform the following actions:</p>

<ul>
	<li><strong>Edit:</strong> Modify your account settings and personal information</li>
	<li><strong>Show Space Explorer:</strong> Display the space hierarchy to explore available spaces</li>
	<li><strong>Manage Trash Bin:</strong> Access and restore resources you have deleted</li>
	<li><strong>Subscribe to Error Logs:</strong> Receive notifications about errors in your jobs (available for developers and administrators)</li>
	<li><strong>Associate Orphaned Primitives:</strong> Link solvers, benchmarks, and jobs that are not in any spaces to appropriate spaces</li>
</ul>
